; kernelx.def — ERA (Xbox One) kernel import lib (phase 5).
; XMemAlloc/XMemFree are a 1:1 map to the GDK xmem.dll functions (same
; API, different module); see docs/ERA-GDK-MAPPING.md.
; Ordinals are the Xbox One shim-DLL kernelx.dll ordinals — the only
; real ordinal layout available. ERA titles import kernelx BY NAME, so
; the ordinal rows never affect a name import; they only matter for a
; title that imports by ordinal. kernelx's other imports in a real ERA
; title are Win32 API names (~106) that the layer forwards to
; kernel32.dll at load time — they are not in this .def because they
; are not layer exports (see src/pe_loader.cpp). VirtualAlloc is the
; one exception to the forward: the layer translates it
; (HleVirtualAlloc, VirtualAlloc flag-translation fix 2026-11-23) via
; the HLE table, NOT via this .def — putting the NAME "VirtualAlloc"
; here would make the era guest link it from kernelx.lib and reroute
; the CRT's own VirtualAlloc calls through the wrapper (kernelx.lib is
; searched before kernel32.lib). Instead the test hook is exported
; under its own name, HleVirtualAlloc, so the era guest can call the
; wrapper directly and unit-test the flag translation while the guest's
; (and the CRT's) plain VirtualAlloc still goes to kernel32. An Xbox
; One title boot is the end-to-end proof that the real
; kernelx!VirtualAlloc import routes to HleVirtualAlloc.
LIBRARY kernelx
EXPORTS
    XMemAlloc @514
    XMemFree @517
    XMemAllocDefault @515
    XMemFreeDefault @518
    XMemSetAllocationHooks @524
    TitleMemoryStatus @463
    HleVirtualAlloc
